    {
      "step": 3,
      "user_message": "Please remember that I spent time with my friend Emily last night discussing our upcoming trip to Italy.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and remember: Please remember that I spent time with my friend Emily last night discussing our upcoming trip to Italy.",
      "agent_response": "Got it — I’ll remember that you spent time with your friend Emily last night discussing your upcoming trip to Italy.\n\nWhat would you like me to do with that memory? Here are some options I can help with next:\n- Draft a follow-up email to Emily (thank-you + next steps / confirm dates / share itinerary ideas). Tell me whether to send now, save as draft, or just copy the text.\n- Search your inbox for Emily (give me how she appears, e.g., “Emily Carter, Travel”) and forward or reply to any relevant messages.\n- Create a short note summarizing what you discussed (dates, places, tasks to book).\n- Remind you to follow up later (if you want a draft reminder email or calendar text I can draft).\n\nIf you want a follow-up email, tell me:\n- Which tone/template (quick thank-you, detailed itinerary plan, or casual check-in).\n- Any specific details to include (trip dates, places you discussed, things to book).\n- Emily’s email or how she appears in your mailbox.\n\nAlso — I still remember your painting (landscape) and the cooking-class note about Mark. Want any of those mentioned in the message to Emily?",
      "duration_s": 12.366,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "user_message": "I enjoyed catching up with my old college friend, Rachel, over brunch at a cozy cafe downtown this morning.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and remember: I enjoyed catching up with my old college friend, Rachel, over brunch at a cozy cafe downtown this morning.",
      "agent_response": "Got it — I’ve saved that you caught up with your college friend Rachel over brunch at a cozy cafe this morning.\n\nWhat would you like me to do next? Options:\n- Draft/send a follow-up email to Rachel (send now / save as draft / just copy the text for you).\n- Search your inbox for Rachel (tell me how she appears, e.g., “Rachel Lee, College”) and reply or forward any relevant messages.\n- Create a short note summarizing the brunch (who, where, topics) or set a reminder to follow up later.\n\nQuick templates — tell me which number to use or say “edit” to change one:\n1) Thank-you + plan another meetup\nHi Rachel —  \nIt was so great catching up at [cafe] this morning! I loved hearing about everything you’ve been up to. Want to do it again soon — maybe next weekend or an evening this week? Let me know what works.  \nCheers,  \n[Your name]\n\n2) Share photos / cafe rec\nHi Rachel —  \nI had a lovely time brunching today — the [cafe name] was perfect. I’m attaching a couple of photos. Want to try that new tapas place next time?  \nBest,  \n[Your name]\n\n3) Casual check-in\nHey Rachel —  \nReally enjoyed catching up this morning — it was like old times! Let’s not wait so long to do it again. 🙂  \n— [Your name]\n\nTell me:\n- Which template (1/2/3 or “edit”), and any text changes.\n- Send now, save as draft, or just copy the text.\n- Rachel’s email address or how she appears in your mailbox.\n- Whether to mention your new painting, the Italy trip, or your cooking-class with Mark in the message.\n\nI’ll take the action once you confirm.",
      "duration_s": 15.982,
      "success_check": null
    },
