    {
      "step": 6,
      "user_message": "I caught up with my cousin Sarah yesterday over a virtual coffee date, and we shared updates on our families.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and remember: I caught up with my cousin Sarah yesterday over a virtual coffee date, and we shared updates on our families.",
      "agent_response": "Got it — I’ve saved that you had a virtual coffee with your cousin Sarah yesterday and you both shared family updates.\n\nWhat would you like me to do next? Options:\n- Draft/send a follow-up email to Sarah (send now / save as draft / just copy the text for you).\n- Search your inbox for Sarah (tell me how she appears, e.g., “Sarah Kim, Cousin”) and reply or forward any relevant messages.\n- Create a short note summarizing your conversation (family updates, any follow-ups).\n- Set a reminder to check in later.\n\nQuick templates — tell me which number to use or say “edit” to change one:\n\n1) Thank-you + follow-up\nHi Sarah —  \nIt was wonderful catching up over virtual coffee yesterday. I loved hearing about everyone — please send my best to [family member]. Let’s do this again soon; are you free next weekend or the week after?  \nLove,  \n[Your name]\n\n2) Share a family photo / update\nHi Sarah —  \nGreat talking yesterday — I enjoyed hearing about the kids and what’s new. I’m attaching a photo from our weekend. Would love any pics you want to share too.  \nTake care,  \n[Your name]\n\n3) Casual check-in\nHey Sarah —  \nReally enjoyed our chat yesterday — felt good to catch up! Let’s not wait too long to do it again. 🙂  \n— [Your name]\n\nTell me:\n- Which template (1/2/3 or “edit”) and any edits you want.\n- Send now, save as draft, or just copy the text.\n- Sarah’s email or how she appears in your mailbox.\n- Whether to mention any other memory (painting, Italy trip, restaurant, Mark) in the message.\n\nI’ll take the action once you confirm.",
      "duration_s": 16.358,
