      "user_message": "I had a great time trying out a new recipe with my friend Jessica at the cooking class last night.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and remember: I had a great time trying out a new recipe with my friend Jessica at the cooking class last night.",
      "agent_response": "Got it — I’ve saved that you tried a new recipe with your friend Jessica at the cooking class last night and had a great time.\n\nWhat would you like me to do with that? Options:\n- Draft/send a follow-up email to Jessica (send now / save as draft / just copy the text for you).\n- Search your inbox for Jessica (tell me how she appears, e.g., “Jessica Park, Design”) and reply or forward any relevant message.\n- Create a short note summarizing the class and the recipe you tried.\n- Set a reminder to follow up or plan another cook-along.\n\nQuick follow-up templates — tell me which number to use or say “edit” to change one:\n\n1) Thank-you + plan another cook session\nHi Jessica —  \nGreat cooking with you last night! I had a lot of fun trying that new recipe. Want to try making it together again sometime this week or next? Let me know what days work for you.  \nCheers,  \n[Your name]\n\n2) Share recipe notes\nHi Jessica —  \nReally enjoyed last night’s class — thanks for being such a fun partner! I tried the recipe again this morning and attached my notes. Want to swap tips or try another recipe next time?  \nBest,  \n[Your name]\n\n3) Casual / keep it light\nHey Jessica —  \nHad a blast cooking last night — that recipe turned out surprisingly well! If you’re up for another class or a cook-along, I’m in. 🙂  \n— [Your name]\n\nTell me:\n- Which template (1/2/3 or “edit”) and any edits.\n- Send now, save as draft, or just copy the text.\n- Jessica’s email address or how she appears in your mailbox.\n- Whether to mention any other memory (your painting, the Italy trip with Emily, brunch with Rachel, the new restaurant) in the message.\n\nI’ll take the action once you confirm.",
      "duration_s": 12.446,
