      "agent_response": "Got it — I’ve saved that you went on a weekend trip to the mountains with your friend Alex and had a great time hiking and exploring the trails.\n\nWhat would you like me to do with this memory? Options:\n- Draft/send a follow-up email to Alex (send now / save as draft / just copy the text). Tell me Alex’s email or how he appears in your mailbox.\n- Search your inbox for Alex and reply/forward any relevant messages.\n- Create a short note summarizing the trip (dates, trails, highlights) for your records.\n- Set a reminder to follow up or plan another hike.\n- Mention the trip in a message to Rachel, Emily, Mark, or someone else.\n\nQuick email templates — tell me which number to use or say “edit” to change one:\n\n1) Thank-you + share photos\nHi Alex —  \nReally enjoyed our mountain trip this weekend — those trails were amazing! Thanks for the company. I’m attaching a couple of photos. Want to plan another hike sometime next month?  \nCheers,  \n[Your name]\n\n2) Plan the next outing\nHey Alex —  \nHad a great time hiking together — want to pick a weekend in [month] for another trip? I’m free [give days/times]. What works for you?  \n— [Your name]\n\n3) Casual check-in\nHi Alex —  \nJust wanted to say I had a blast this weekend — let’s do it again soon!  \nBest,  \n[Your name]\n\nTell me:\n- Which action and template (1/2/3 or “edit”).\n- Send now, save as draft, or copy only.\n- Alex’s email or how he appears in your mailbox.\n- Any details to include (dates, favorite trail, photos, availability) or whether to mention other memories.",
